IMHO... No, there is not.

Nethack was started as a for-fun project by geeks in the 1980's. They
probably enjoyed it for a long time, but my guess is that it's since
evolved into a major stressor for them. Imagine the first program you
wanted to write after you learned to program in C. Then imagine a
million fans telling you it's not good enough, and to hurry up.
Imagine these complaints posted on slashdot every year, and then one
of your teammates dies. Usenet, which was once your previous stomping
ground, now constantly demeans your work. The Dev Team's college
pastime probably doesn't seem to hold the same importance for them
anymore.

My guess is that it's probably time for a major variant. Some people
have already tried this. Rogue begat Hack and Hack begat Nethack. It's
time for the rest of us to accept a change in ownership.

